  "description": "AsyncFixer detects common async/await anti-patterns and, when possible, offers automatic fixes. It currently reports 6 categories of async/await misuse and provides code fixes for 3 of them. It has been validated against thousands of open-source C# projects and is designed to handle tricky real-world edge cases. Tool-friendly diagnostics support AI-assisted workflows even when a built-in code fix is not available.",
